<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deo Van Long</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1887">1887</a>–<a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deo Van Long was a White Tai chief from Lai Châu in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> who allied with the French against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>. In 1948 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> made him head of the autonomous Tai Federation. After the French defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> in 1954 the federation ended and he went into exile in France.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/deo-van-long.jpg" alt="Deo Van Long" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kinodo2 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SA_Deo_Van_Long_-_Lai_Chau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
